<!--
    A declared 64-bit return in a register pair beside another call's
    result (#1921).  clang 20 -O2 (i386), of

        long long ext64(int c, int k);                  declared below
        long long pair64(int c, int k) {
            if (mb() == 1) return ext64(c, k);          jmp ext64
            if (c < 0) return partner64(-c, k);
            point += c; return 0;
        }

    Narrowing a returned call's output (`try_call_return_push`) acts only
    where the RETURN consumes less than the call writes.  Here the declared
    result fills edx:eax, so nothing marks fewer bytes consumed: the return
    stays the whole pair and the unlocked partner's edx:eax is kept whole.

    Stage / sub-stage: P3 "subvariable flow".  No option.
-->
